# P18-V02 final local rerun and request-reply deadline race fix — 2026-10-17T04:29:09Z

- Code commit: `e9fe95cd fix(request-reply): expire entries at captured deadline`.
  The repeated race smoke exposed that the registry sweep used only the future's
  relative timeout, which can drift from the captured request deadline when
  registration is delayed. Expiration now honors the stored absolute deadline
  as well; a regression extends the future timeout after registration and
  verifies that the registry still expires at the request deadline.
- Final server-free gates passed on `e9fe95cd`: `TZ=UTC cargo test
  --workspace --locked`; `TZ=UTC cargo test --workspace --all-features
  --locked`; strict all-target/all-feature workspace Clippy; pinned Maven
  `verify` (37 scenarios, fixture checks, Java/Rust cross-decodes); comparator
  self-test and 37-scenario manifest validation; race/leak smoke (16 cases ×
  3); fuzz smoke (105 frame seeds, 11 message seeds, 1,856 mutations); release
  examples; workspace benchmark compilation; workspace metadata/license/
  dependency checks; seven package listings with LICENSE and NOTICE; format and
  diff checks.
- The first post-change race-smoke run reproduced the flaky timeout assertion
  on repetition 3. The absolute-deadline correction and focused regression
  passed, then the complete 16 × 3 smoke rerun passed. The initial full-workspace
  test command's shell wrapper used zsh's read-only `status` variable after the
  tests had completed; the workspace suites were rerun with a corrected wrapper
  and both returned exit code 0. No test failure remained.
- P18-V02 server-free gates are complete on this code revision. P18-V01's broad
  source/API/settings/overload/error/control-flow/reverse-export audit remains
  open. The 37-scenario manifest is valid, but the Phase 19 Docker/Broker
  runner and local scenario execution remain automatic work, not manual
  validation.
